      "stage": "Early focused user probe",
      "work": "Use the already permitted supervised probe of the current Coverage Table to observe whether a coordinator recognizes an unfilled period before deciding to download. This can proceed independently of construction. Bind the view, scenario, user capability and observation; retain any assistance or uncertainty.",
      "claim_limit": "This answers the specific recognition question. It supplies neither full-capability acceptance nor authority to change requirements. A demonstrated display nonconformance can lead to bounded repair under the existing meaning."
    },
    {
      "stage": "First construction increment",
      "work": "Correct I4's excluded-end behavior and connect the selected participants. Use C2-derived boundary cases and the smallest adequate module-law populations. Reuse E1/E2 where applicable and observe the changed intake/adapter/planner and table/exporter seams.",
      "claim_limit": "Component laws and exercised interfaces retain separate evidence scopes."
    },
